  "panels": [
    {
      "content": "## AKS control-plane etcd (hyperscale-aware)\\n\\nOn **hyperscale** control planes etcd is split into **6 independent partitions** (`etcd`, `etcd-events`, `etcd-leases`, `etcd-nodes`, `etcd-pods`, `etcd-secrets`), each with **3 Raft replicas**. The `controlplane-etcd` scrape job emits one flat series per member distinguished only by `instance` (the pod name, e.g. `etcd-nodes-<ccp>-<rand>`) and adds **no** partition label, so `etcd_mvcc_db_total_size_in_bytes` arrives as up to 18 flat series.\\n\\nThese two dimensions need **opposite** aggregation:\\n\\n- The **6 partitions are disjoint** keyspaces \\u2192 they **SUM** (total DB size).\\n- The **3 replicas** in a partition are Raft **duplicates** of the same data \\u2192 they must be **collapsed with `max`**, never summed.\\n\\nSo `sum(etcd_mvcc_db_total_size_in_bytes)` over-reports ~3x and `max(...)` under-reports (only the biggest partition). Every panel here derives an `etcd_partition` label from `instance` via `label_replace`, does **max-over-replicas first**, then **sum-over-partitions**. Non-hyperscale clusters have a single `etcd` partition and behave correctly with the same math.\\n\\n> Regex note: in the `label_replace` alternation the specific `etcd-<name>` branches come **before** the bare `etcd` (Go RE2 is leftmost-first) \\u2013 otherwise `etcd-nodes-\\u2026` would wrongly capture just `etcd`.\\n\\nPanels prefer the recorded rules from `etcd-RecordingRules.json` and fall back to the raw `label_replace` expression (via `or`) when the rule group is not deployed.",
      "datasource": null,
      "description": "How the numbers are computed.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 2,
      "mode": "markdown",
      "span": 12,
      "title": "Why partition-aware math?",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
  "refresh": "1m",
